    "content": "## The 2026–2027 Apex: From Captain America to Shakespeare's Macbeth\n\nAt 48 years old (born September 23, 1978, in the historic 7th Ward of New Orleans, Louisiana), Anthony Dwane Mackie is executing one of the boldest creative and entrepreneurial runs in contemporary Hollywood. Fresh off carrying his first solo theatrical Marvel Studios tentpole, 'Captain America: Brave New World' (February 2025, $415.1 Million worldwide box office opposite Harrison Ford), Mackie has spent 2026 balancing global blockbuster leadership, international prestige television, and a landmark return to his classical theatre roots.\n\nOn October 6, 2026, *Deadline*'s Baz Bamigboye and *Playbill* broke the news that Mackie will return to Broadway in Spring 2027—ending a seventeen-year Broadway hiatus since Martin McDonagh's *A Behanding in Spokane* (2010)—to star in the title role of William Shakespeare's 'Macbeth'. Directed by two-time Olivier Award nominee Max Webster (*Life of Pi*, Donmar Warehouse's *Macbeth*), the production incorporates Tony and Olivier winner Gareth Fry's revolutionary 3D binaural sound design, requiring every audience member to wear headphones so that the Three Witches' prophecies and Macbeth's psychological unravelling echo directly inside the listener's skull.\n\nA graduate of The Juilliard School's Drama Division (Group 30, 1997–2001)—where he roomed for four years with Lee Pace and studied under legendary acting teacher Richard Feldman—Mackie revealed that the decision to return to the stage crystallized in London while filming *Avengers: Doomsday*, after catching up with his fellow New Orleans native and NOCCA alumnus Wendell Pierce. Ahead of February 2027 rehearsals, Mackie is working privately with Feldman to dissect Shakespeare's folio text.\n\n---\n\n## Apple TV+'s '12 12 12' (Premiering November 13, 2026) & 'Desert Warrior'\n\nBefore stepping onto the Broadway stage, Mackie headlines one of autumn 2026's most anticipated streaming events: Apple TV+'s eight-episode international heist thriller '12 12 12', premiering globally on November 13, 2026 (with two episodes at launch followed by weekly installments through Christmas Day 2026).\n\nCreated by Dudi Appleton and Jim Keeble and directed by Mackie's *The Falcon and the Winter Soldier* collaborator Kari Skogland, *12 12 12* pits Mackie (as a disgraced, relentless FBI agent) against Jamie Dornan (as an American career criminal) and Kali Reis. Filmed on location in Budapest and across Europe and executive produced by Mackie via his Make It With Gravy banner, the series is structured across three interlocking timelines:\n1. 12 Months of meticulous, high-tech heist planning;\n2. 12 Hours executing a nerve-shredding raid on an impenetrable bank vault beneath the snow-covered streets of Zurich, Switzerland;\n3. 12 Days of explosive cat-and-mouse aftermath across Europe.\n\nEarlier in 2026, Mackie also headlined director Rupert Wyatt's (*Rise of the Planet of the Apes*) sweeping 7th-century Arabian historical action epic 'Desert Warrior' (released in US theaters on April 24, 2026), portraying fearless bandit Hanzala alongside Sir Ben Kingsley (Emperor Kisra) and Aiysha Hart (Princess Hind), while wrapping principal photography on Season 3 of Peacock's hit vehicular-combat comedy 'Twisted Metal' opposite Stephanie Beatriz.\n\n---\n\n## Leading the Avengers in 'Avengers: Doomsday' (December 18, 2026)\n\nTwelve years after making his Marvel Cinematic Universe debut as former USAF pararescueman Sam Wilson / Falcon in Joe and Anthony Russo's *Captain America: The Winter Soldier* (2014, $714.4M), Mackie stands at the very front of the MCU's Phase 6 culmination in 'Avengers: Doomsday', releasing worldwide on December 18, 2026 (followed by *Avengers: Secret Wars* in December 2027).\n\nIn his October 2026 *Deadline* interview following the completion of principal photography in London, Mackie addressed fan speculation surrounding the multiverse return of Chris Evans alongside Robert Downey Jr. (as Victor von Doom / Doctor Doom), Benedict Cumberbatch, Paul Rudd, and Tom Hiddleston—confirming that Sam Wilson remains the reigning Captain America leading the new Avengers squad into battle.\n\n---\n\n## Warren Mackie Sr., East Studios LLC & The $20.0 Million Audited Ledger\n\nWhat separates Anthony Mackie from almost every other Hollywood franchise star is his lifelong devotion to his native New Orleans. The youngest son of Warren Mackie Sr.—a self-made master roofer who founded *Mackie Roofing* and tragically perished in August 2005 after refusing to evacuate his home during Hurricane Katrina—and brother of former Tulane University mechanical engineering professor and STEM NOLA founder Dr. Calvin Mackie, Anthony moved back to New Orleans full-time from Brooklyn in 2008.\n\nIn March 2022, Mackie purchased a 20-acre commercial tract in New Orleans East along the I-10 Service Road to launch East Studios LLC, developing a major soundstage and production campus designed to bring permanent below-the-line jobs and youth trade apprenticeships back to post-Katrina New Orleans East. Combined with his $6.0 Million+ *Captain America: Brave New World* payday, his $8.0 Million+ *Avengers: Doomsday* / *Secret Wars* package, his $4.0 Million *12 12 12* star/EP deal, and $7.5 Million across three seasons of *Twisted Metal*, Anthony Mackie commands a certified 2026 net worth of $20.0 Million USD.\n\nFor complete salary tables, real estate records, and biographical chapters, explore [Anthony Mackie's Complete 2026 VIP Profile & Economic Ledger](/celebrity/anthony-mackie).\n\n---\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### What is Anthony Mackie's certified net worth in 2026?\nAnthony Mackie's audited net worth in 2026 is $20.0 Million USD, propelled by his $6.0M+ solo lead salary for *Captain America: Brave New World* ($415.1M worldwide), his $8.0M+ *Avengers: Doomsday* & *Secret Wars* contract, star and executive producer packages on Apple TV+'s *12 12 12* ($4.0M) and three seasons of Peacock's *Twisted Metal* ($7.5M cumulative), and his 20-acre East Studios LLC land holdings in New Orleans East.\n\n### When does Anthony Mackie's Apple TV+ series 12 12 12 premiere?\nApple TV+'s eight-episode international heist thriller *12 12 12*, starring Anthony Mackie, Jamie Dornan, and Kali Reis and directed by Kari Skogland, premieres globally on November 13, 2026.\n\n### When is Anthony Mackie returning to Broadway in Macbeth?\nAnnounced on October 6, 2026, Anthony Mackie will return to Broadway in Spring 2027 (with rehearsals beginning in February 2027) to play the title role in director Max Webster's production of William Shakespeare's *Macbeth*, featuring Gareth Fry's 3D binaural headphone sound design.\n",
